    {
     "type": "textmedia",
     "header": "<h1> A short look at five common mistakes and ZOLLER's solutions </h1>",
     "body": "<p><strong>Small businesses, especially, are hesitant to digitize their manufacturing processes and, as a result, unnecessarily forgo significant efficiency advantages over their competitors. These hesitations are often rooted in misconceptions. It’s high time to dispel some of these misconceptions and, at the same time, present suitable solutions for small and medium-sized manufacturing operations.</strong></p> <p>Digitalization is all about efficiency. Digitalization is always a win when it makes processes simpler, faster, more cost-effective, or more safe. This principle applies to large, medium, and small manufacturing operations alike. If a digital tool helps a company gain an efficiency edge, the investment is worth it.</p> <p>Small businesses often perceive the effort required for digitalization as too great and the benefits as too low. But the fact is: Nearly every manufacturing operation has opportunities for digitalization.</p>",
     "images": [],
     "videos": [],
     "pos": "text",
     "cols": 1,
     "valign": "top",
     "ftype": "text",
     "id": "c99119",
     "bg": "",
     "space": {
      "before": "default",
      "after": "default"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "textmedia",
     "header": "",
